      "writtenOn": "2026-08-31T16:34:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, as a pure user of the API, I probably would expect that. The UI however doesn\u0027t show Included In except for merged changes, and that\u0027s always been the case. I\u0027m now really viewing this more as a disconnect between how the API is expected to be used and what\u0027s actually allowed, so perhaps my [initial change](https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/c/gerrit/+/622941) that returns a 409 is a better approach. If someone just wants to know if a commit is in a branch/tag/ref, we have `/project/` APIs available for that.\n\nDoes that make sense to you?",
      "parentUuid": "1a00ebba_57ec9fc1",
      "revId": "6f6983b01484263f9c40c91503409b2e95f47f4d",
